## What is Recursion?

Recursion is a method where the solution to a problem depends on solutions to smaller instances of the same problem.

### Base Case
The base case is the condition that stops the recursion. Without it, the function would call itself infinitely.

### Recursive Case
The recursive case is the part of the function that calls itself with a smaller or simpler input.

```
function recursiveFunction(input):
  if (base case condition):
    return base_value
  else:
    return recursiveFunction(smaller_input)
```

